// Test fixture: one conversation per mistake the loader has to catch, and one that is fine.
// Compile with: ysc compile checks.yarn -o . -n checks

title: Fine
kind: Greeting
attach: Speaker.Role == guard
---
Guard: Move along. #line:fine_move
You: Moving. #line:fine_moving
===

title: UnknownFunction
kind: Greeting
attach: Speaker.Role == guard
---
<<if wealth() > 3>>
    Guard: Rich, are you? #line:unknown_function_rich
<<endif>>
===

title: UnknownCommand
kind: Greeting
attach: Speaker.Role == guard
---
Guard: Take this. #line:unknown_command_take
<<GiveGold 5>>
===

title: WrongCount
kind: Greeting
attach: Speaker.Role == guard
---
Guard: Pay up. #line:wrong_count_pay
<<TakeMoney>>
===

title: WrongArity
kind: Greeting
attach: Speaker.Role == guard
---
<<if flag()>>
    Guard: I know you. #line:wrong_arity_know
<<endif>>
===

title: BadReason
kind: Greeting
attach: Speaker.Role == guard
---
Guard: Well? #line:bad_reason_well
-> Bribe him. <<if gold() >= 5>> #line:bad_reason_bribe #reason:too_poor
-> Leave. #line:bad_reason_leave
===

title: Untagged
kind: Greeting
attach: Speaker.Role == guard
---
Guard: This line was never given an id.
===

title: UsesBroken
kind: Greeting
attach: Speaker.Role == guard
---
Guard: Let me check. #line:uses_broken_check
<<jump Broken>>
===

title: Broken
---
<<Explode>>
===

title: BadKind
kind: Banter
attach: Speaker.Role == guard
---
Guard: Hm. #line:bad_kind_hm
===

title: NoAttach
kind: Greeting
---
Guard: Who are you? #line:no_attach_who
===

title: TopicNoLabel
kind: Topic
attach: Speaker.Role == guard
---
Guard: About that. #line:topic_no_label_about
===
